","known_bad_label":"Only shallow-copies chapters, leaving returned keyword slices aliased to the input."},{"id":"cap-v2-parsing_and_encoding-go-generation-01","problem":"Implement a parser for an in-memory badge manifest.

Use package `solution` and provide this public API:

```go
type Badge struct {
    Name string
    Rank int
    Note string
}

func ParseBadgeManifest(text string) ([]Badge, error)
```

The manifest consists of LF-separated lines. Empty lines are ignored. Every non-empty line must contain exactly three fields separated by literal `|` bytes:

```text
encoded-name|rank|encoded-note
```

`encoded-name` and `encoded-note` use percent encoding: `%` must be followed by exactly two hexadecimal digits representing one byte. Decode these fields using URL path semantics, so `+` remains `+`. Encoded bytes may form UTF-8 text, including an encoded `|`. The decoded name must be non-empty, while the decoded note may be empty. Both decoded strings must be valid UTF-8.

`rank` must contain only ASCII decimal digits and represent an integer from 0 through 100 inclusive. A wrong field count, bad percent escape, invalid UTF-8, empty name, invalid rank syntax, overflow, or out-of-range rank must return a non-nil error and no partial result. Preserve record order and return an empty non-nil slice for an empty manifest.

Use only the Go standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness. Return a complete source file without a `main` function.","reference_code":"package solution

import (
	"fmt"
	"net/url"
	"strconv"
	"strings"
	"unicode/utf8"
)

type Badge struct {
	Name string
	Rank int
	Note string
}

func ParseBadgeManifest(text string) ([]Badge, error) {
	badges := make([]Badge, 0)
	for index, line := range strings.Split(text, "\n") {
		if line == "" {
			continue
		}

		fields := strings.Split(line, "|")
		if len(fields) != 3 {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: expected three fields", index+1)
		}

		name, err := decodeBadgeField(fields[0])
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: invalid name: %w", index+1, err)
		}
		if name == "" {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: empty name", index+1)
		}

		if !decimalDigits(fields[1]) {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: invalid rank", index+1)
		}
		rank, err := strconv.Atoi(fields[1])
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: invalid rank: %w", index+1, err)
		}
		if rank < 0 || rank > 100 {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: rank out of range", index+1)
		}

		note, err := decodeBadgeField(fields[2])
		if err != nil {
			return nil, fmt.Errorf("line %d: invalid note: %w", index+1, err)
		}

		badges = append(badges, Badge{Name: name, Rank: rank, Note: note})
	}
	return badges, nil
}

func decodeBadgeField(encoded string) (string, error) {
	decoded, err := url.PathUnescape(encoded)
	if err != nil {
		return "", err
	}
	if !utf8.ValidString(decoded) {
		return "", fmt.Errorf("decoded value is not valid UTF-8")
	}
	return decoded, nil
}

func decimalDigits(value string) bool {
	if value == "" {
		return false
	}
	for i := 0; i < len(value); i++ {
		if value[i] < '0' || value[i] > '9' {
			return false
		}
	}
	return true
}
